# PRM - Please Remind Me

Environment variables. Copy this file to `.env` and adjust if needed.
By default PRM is still **local-first**: user data lives in the browser's
IndexedDB and never leaves the device. Phase 2 (see backend/.env.example)
adds an optional backend; VITE_STORAGE_MODE below is the only thing that
switches the frontend over to it.

## App
# Environment: development | production
APP_ENV=development

# Port used by the local preview/dev server and the Docker container
APP_PORT=8000

## Public URL (optional)
# Base public URL where the app is served. Used for the PWA scope/start_url.
# Leave empty for same-origin serving (recommended for OMV/NAS static hosting).
APP_BASE_URL=

## Phase 2 storage adapter (optional — see backend/)
# 'http' talks to the backend API instead of the browser's IndexedDB; any
# other value (or leaving it unset) keeps phase 1's on-device storage.
# Attachments always stay on-device either way (see src/types/index.ts).
VITE_STORAGE_MODE=indexeddb

# Base URL for the backend API when VITE_STORAGE_MODE=http. Leave as '/api'
# when the backend serves the built PWA itself (same container, same origin
# — see Dockerfile), which is the normal deployed setup.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
prm.m03z.com
